    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table, surfaced on the owner response (`GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper mirroring the existing `HouseholdId` pattern, holding the pinned table `Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD` and a static `of(city)` returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other (or null) city.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `locality`, computed via `Locality.of(owner.getCity())`, alongside the other derived fields.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (both the known-city `Sydney\u2192NSW` and unknown-city\u2192`UNKNOWN` cases) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
